{
  "note": "Rejudged 2026-10-23 by an independent auditor (not the author) after 010e649057, which makes the final writer (session_ownership.go adjOutWrite.allow) send a synthesized withdrawal only to a destination holding an adj-out record for the route. RFC 4271 Section 3.1 allows a withdrawal only for \"the IP prefix that expresses the destination for a previously advertised route\". RFC 2545 Section 3: \"A BGP speaker shall advertise to its peer in the Network Address of Next Hop field the global IPv6 address of the next hop, potentially followed by the link-local IPv6 address of the next hop.\" The one moved unit is TestRFC2545ReceivedUnusableGlobalRefused (both tags): it now calls advertiseFirst, which plants the same route in the destination's adj-out through the raw session writer (ownershipWriterForward, bypassing the forward gates) and clears the socket, before the received UPDATE is forwarded. Every assertion is unchanged: exactly one recipient UPDATE; for usable globals (single and paired) an exact MP_REACH with the received next hop; for unspecified and multicast globals (single and paired, with and without capability 77) no MP_REACH and the exact MP_UNREACH; no legacy NLRI. Bypassing the unusable-global egress gate would send an announcement and fail; rejecting every IPv6 next hop would withdraw the valid cases and fail; so the negative (never announced) and positive (usable global advertised) both still discriminate. The planted earlier generation carries the invalid hop itself; that is fixture state that makes the withdrawal legitimate, not a claim about Ze's output. The changed helper rfc2545ReceiveForwardPublished primes adj-out only where it expects a gate withdrawal; its tagged callers are byte-identical and keep their prior judgement. Every other tagged carrier named by the 2026-10-22 verdict is byte-identical and its judgement stands (scoped origination wrappers, builder/forward admission, link-local append when Section 3 holds, SR Policy wire, encode/exabgp/plugin .ci). Ran: go test reactor -run TestRFC2545ReceivedUnusableGlobalRefused and TestRFC4659LinkLocalPeeringPreservesUnspecifiedGlobalPair, PASS on 2026-10-23 working tree.",
